--[[
The Seagate: the gatehouse on the seawall, where the stairs from the frontier come down. A fire in the stair hall (the
first rest in the city), and from the balcony, the whole city far below: its roofs, its towers, the palace on its cliff.
The plaza of the gate is swept by a crimson lens (it always sees): seen, the place locks down and hounds come out of the
hatches. The great Seagate (the lift down to the Ward) is shut: the guards kept it up. The way down is the drain of the
guard room, a pipe that comes out in the water tower of the Ward. From the Ward, the lever of the guard post brings the
lift down: a shortcut, for later. A crack in the north wall of the stair hall hides the cache of the guards.
]]
